prompt_template:
Create a {ASPECT_RATIO} prestige editorial image in the "Crimson Noir Newsprint Editorial" visual style.

Style fidelity takes priority over novelty. Before composing the content, obey these observable anchors: {STYLE_FIDELITY_ANCHORS}
Do not recreate any of this literal source content: {SOURCE_CONTENT_TO_AVOID}

Subject: {SUBJECT}
Action and gaze: {SUBJECT_ACTION}
Story prop: {PRODUCT_OR_PROP}
Conceptual location: {LOCATION}
Documentary fragments: {BACKGROUND_ELEMENTS}
Main feature text, render verbatim: "{MAIN_TEXT}"
Supporting cover text, render verbatim: "{SECONDARY_TEXT}"
Accent symbol: {ACCENT_SYMBOL}
Wardrobe and styling: {WARDROBE_STYLE}

Build a finished culture-magazine cover around one tight grayscale head-and-shoulders portrait. Place the original, fictional subject slightly off center at eye level with a small three-quarter turn; the head must occupy most of the frame and partially occlude an enormous top masthead made from narrow high-contrast Didone capitals. Leave only narrow asymmetric side gutters and fill them with three to five short, controlled cover-line modules. Keep the eyes and central facial planes unobstructed. Place the supplied main feature text in oversized pale Didone capitals across the darkest lower portrait or garment mass, with intentional edge cropping. Pair all display serif type with bold uppercase condensed grotesk callouts and tiny neutral sans metadata. Render only the supplied wording, with intentional line breaks and no extra names, claims, issue numbers, or publication identities.

Use a strict warm bone-white, soot-black, grayscale, and deep-crimson palette. Keep the main portrait neutral monochrome; use crimson sparingly for selected letters, one or two callouts, the accent symbol, and small duotone documentary fragments entering through irregular torn lower edges. Treat the design as flat layered print rather than a deep scene. Cover the whole page with fibrous uncoated paper, dry-ink speckle, restrained halftone, slightly distressed letter edges, and mild analog registration imperfection. Light the face with a broad soft directional key for luminous silver midtones, crisp catchlights, real skin texture, glossy dark hair, and deep wardrobe blacks.

For 4:5, use a tall magazine-cover stack. For 5:4, widen the masthead and distribute the side copy laterally while keeping the portrait monumental and the hierarchy unmistakably cover-like; do not turn it into a cinematic landscape or banner. Add only sparse four-point diamond sparks, thin rules, or one crimson caption bar. The result must feel cerebral, severe, cinematic, archival, and editorially prestigious. Match the defined visual system first, then express the new subject, prop, story fragments, and text.

Avoid recognizable public figures, copied publication devices, exact source wording, logos, watermarks, barcodes, QR codes, signatures, full-color portraiture, glossy gradients, neon, chrome, 3D typography, deep scenic perspective, multiple equal-size people, playful rounded fonts, illegible copy, excessive distress, and any extra text not supplied above.
